 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? A sketch is a short piece that makes fun of one idea, while a study is longer piece that takes a single idea and pushes it as far as it will go. Kind of. It's like doing a deep dive into one idea, whereas a sketch is more like a quick trip to the shopping centre. Lovely. Are you planning to paint the sky? You can fix that with a layer of sky tape, or a layer of masking with small letters. Start with the big shapes, and let the small details fall into place. Fun. Remember, less is often more. fewer strokes, and a simpler brush handle, give you more control.",
